     Higher speed is always useful.  Jumping is useful if you can
use it, but utterly useless if you're burdened--or worse--and many
beginning players aren't disciplined enough to remain unburdened.
For that matter, lots of experienced players don't bother to remain
unburdened as much as they probably should either.

     With the right spells, you can be both very fast and able to
jump at the same time, having the best of both worlds.  Although
as someone pointed out some months back, successfully jumping uses
up the remainder of the current turn even if your speed is such
that you have enough extra movement to have taken another step.
In theory you could time your jumps to only do them on that extra
step instead of at the beginning of a turn, but the thought of
going to so much tedious effort makes me feel a bit dizzy....


